		PRINTFORML 「Guided by the natural human drive for growth, it becomes like a purifying drug.」
		PRINTFORML 「The "heart aspiring to enlightenment" drives out the body's impurities without even noticing its presence.」
		PRINTFORML 「And so without even realizing we have the "heart aspiring to enlightenment", we preserve the purity of our mind.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Here, the "impurities" I speak of are temptation and malice opposing the "heart aspiring to enlightenment".」
		PRINTFORML 
		PRINTFORML 「But there is no such thing as an all-powerful elixir. Each time the drug purifies the body, something undesirable is also formed.」
		PRINTFORML 「The residue of the malice purified by the "heart aspiring to enlightenment" is the suffering from hardship.」
		PRINTFORML 「When you face this suffering without being discouraged, and follow it to its source...」
		PRINTFORMW 「Without doubt, you will find that it is the "heart aspiring to enlightenment". You must follow this heart to discover the virtuous path.」
		PRINTFORML 
		PRINTFORML 「There is a concept of the "pain of rebirth". When old life gives birth to new life, there will always be tears and suffering.」
		PRINTFORML 「When a new bud sprouts from a tree, it must begin by tearing the tree's skin. This is the suffering. And the tree's sap...」
		PRINTFORMW 「These are the tears. From the tears and suffering, the new life of Spring bursts forth.」
	CASE 2
		PRINTFORMW 「Let's see... What do you think about "likes and dislikes"?」
		PRINTFORML 
		PRINTFORML 「As long as a person possesses a heart of emotion, that person will naturally grow to prefer some things and dislike other things.」
		PRINTFORML 「This is nothing to rebuke. After all, it is the variety of cherry blossom trees, plum trees, and bamboo that leads to beautiful scenery.」
		PRINTFORML 「In the same way, each person's preferences influences their growth and lifestyle, and that makes us interesting.」
		PRINTFORMW 「The world is not painted in simple monotone. Therefore, having a wide variety of preferences is a wonderful thing.」
		PRINTFORML 
		PRINTFORML 「But there is something regarding these preferences I must not neglect to mention.」
		PRINTFORML 「We must not become prisoners of our preferences. Once we allow our preferences to become stubbornness, we become selfish.」
		PRINTFORML 「For example, "I will not become friends with that person because I don't like them."」
		PRINTFORML 「"Therefore, other people must also not become friends with that person." This kind of thinking is nothing but selfishness.」
		PRINTFORML 「"I don't like pine trees, so they should all disappear from this world."」
		PRINTFORML 「"I love bamboo, so it should become the only plant in the world." This is the same.」
		PRINTFORMW 「If nothing but bamboo were to grow even in Gensokyo, the scenery would become quite dull indeed.」
		PRINTFORML 
		PRINTFORML 「People are the same.」
		PRINTFORML 「"I don't like that person, but others may see them in a better light, so they should become friends."」
		PRINTFORML 「Accepting this, and keeping one's preferences as their own, is the right way.」
		PRINTFORML 「Using one's own dislikes to persecute another, even going so far as to obstruct their happiness, can only be selfishness.」
		PRINTFORML 「Disrupting the world's balance like this is an unforgivable act.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Those who fall into such habits will find themselves driven into a corner by their own hand.」
		PRINTFORML 
